m compose.test.ts's \"rolls funnel counts up from artifacts\" test and deleted its sibling test that was entirely about note_funnel citation counters. projectCache (ProjectorContext.cache_hit_rates/fact_store_reuse) was left alone: those two optional context fields are pure-function inputs unrelated to any deleted artifact shape, still exercised directly by unit tests in projectors.test.ts, so they are not the same class of dead-input bug -- out of the two named projectors' scope.",
 "configOrphans": "Removed both `learning` and `memory` blocks from pipeline/pipeline-config.json (both nested under top-level `thresholds`). Grep dossier for `learning`: `grep -rn \"config\\.learning\\|\\.learning\\.autoApprove\\|autoApprove\\b\" src/` and a broader `grep -rn \"\\blearning\\b\" pipeline/src` (excluding run-summary/ and test/) returned zero live consumers -- only two comments in index.ts noting the learning-record pass was deleted by C5, and one comment in dossier/src (out of scope) mentioning the ADR-0040 threshold by name, never reading it. Grep dossier for `memory`: `grep -rn \"config\\.memory\\|resolveMemoryRelationsConfig\\|\\.memory\\.relations\\|\\.memory\\.junkFractionWarn\\|memoryJunkWarning\\|DEFAULT_MEMORY_JUNK_FRACTION_WARN\" pipeline/src` returned zero reads of config.memory.* -- the only two hits were memoryJunkWarning/DEFAULT_MEMORY_JUNK_FRACTION_WARN's own definitions in run-summary/projectors.ts and an import of both names in index.ts that is never called (a separate, already-dangling import I flagged but did not touch, since it's not itself a config.memory read and wasn't in the named scope). PipelineConfig.learning and .memory are both declared optional (`learning?:`, presumably `memory?:`) in shared/src/types.ts, so removing the JSON blocks does not require any type change; `pipeline-config.json` still parses as valid JSON after the edit and typecheck/tests stayed green. `retrieveDispatch` (sibling block) and `builderFunnel`/`judges` were untouched -- retrieveDispatch/builderFunnel were not named in scope and I found no reason to suspect them dead.",
