 "noteIdFootprint": "After my edits, `grep -rIln \"note_id\\|note_ids\" src/ | grep -v \"src/eval/\"` returns 7 files: report.ts, citation-lint.ts, linting.ts, retrieve-report-contract.ts, lint-warning-channel.ts, steps/analyze.ts (all confirmed comment-only, matching the six accepted DO-NOT-TOUCH rename-explaining files) plus run-summary/projectors.ts. The projectors.ts hit is NOT from projectNoteFunnel or projectEventImpact (both fully deleted, confirmed by function-name grep returning zero hits) -- it is two lines inside the still-alive, out-of-scope projectRetrievalQuality: `d['graph_note_ids']` and `d['orphan_note_ids']` (substring matches on \"note_ids\" inside longer identifier names), used to compute `notes_reached_by_graph` / `notes_reached_by_orphan_scan` from the retrieve-graph diagnostics artifact. This function was not named in my task's item list, so I left it untouched. Flagging as a genuine additional finding for the coordinator: `retrieve-graph-build.ts` was deleted by C5 (confirmed: config.ts's StepName type and its own header comment both list `retrieve_graph_build` among the deleted stages, and it no longer appears in STEP_ORDER), so `artifacts['retrieve-graph']`/`artifacts['retrieve_graph_build']` can never exist again; separately, the surviving `retrieve` step's actual return shape (checked in steps/retrieve.ts) no longer includes a `quality_verdict` field at all, so `readRetrieveQualityVerdict(artifacts['retrieve'])` in compose.ts is also now always undefined. That means projectRetrievalQuality's entire body (both its retrieve_graph-derived fields and its retrieve_quality_verdict-derived themes_total field) is dead-input code of the exact same class as the two projectors I removed -- but it was not in my assigned scope, so I did not touch it. This is very likely a real P4/P5 finding for a follow-up ticket (removal would need the same RunSummary.retrieval_quality required-vs-optional schema check I did for note_funnel/event_impact).",
 "suiteAttribution": "Full suite: 9 failed files | 192 passed | 1 skipped (202 total files); 7 failed | 1781 passed | 4 skipped (1792 total tests). All 9 failing files are exactly the C6-owned set named in the ticket, verified one-by-one: (1-7) the 7 external-benchmark-*.test.ts files (external-benchmark-adapter-seam, -baseline-regression, -benchone-full-pass, -benchone-retrieval, -benchtwo-adapter, -benchtwo-baseline, -isolation-guard) -- all fail on `Cannot find module '../../src/services/dossier/dossierq-client.js'` or missing benchtwo corpus cache, i.e. need the deleted dossier package / stored benchtwo corpus, exactly as described; (8) test/dossier-boundary-doc-consistency.test.ts -- fails on REPO_ROOT not containing 'feed-extractor' (this worktree's checkout path) and ENOENT on the deleted pipeline/cli/dossier-writer.ts, both pre-existing/unrelated to my edits; (9) test/eval/runner.test.ts -- fails asserting extractStep.passed===true (got false), the note-coupled eval / extract-lint-removal failure the ticket names as C6/D2B-7's to fix. Zero new C5-owned failures; the failing-file set is identical to before my change. The passed-file count dropped 194->192 and skipped-file count 2->1 purely because I deleted 3 test files that existed only to test the two removed projectors: 2 of those (event-impact-primary-confirmed.test.ts, event-impact-impact-cards.test.ts) were previously-passing files (194->192), and 1 (run-summary-note-funnel-citations-real-artifact.test.ts) was a previously fully-skipped file in this environment (its it.skip branch fires when the referenced real-run artifacts are absent), accounting for the skipped-file drop from 2 to 1 (test/validate-non-substantive-canary-real-artifact.test.ts is the remaining conditionally-skipped file). At the test level, passed dropped from 1803 to 1781 (-22), which reconciles exactly against the tests I deliberately removed alongside the dead functions: 13 tests from projectors.test.ts's projectNoteFunnel + projectNoteFunnel-citation-counters + projectEventImpact describe blocks, 1 test from compose.test.ts's note_funnel-citation-counters test, 5 tests from event-impact-primary-confirmed.test.ts, 3 tests from event-impact-impact-cards.test.ts (13+1+5+3=22). No other test anywhere newly failed, newly skipped, or changed outcome.",
 "deviations": "(1) Beyond the exact function names in item 2, I also had to delete/trim 3 test files' worth of coverage for projectNoteFunnel/projectEventImpact (2 files deleted in full, 1 file's assertions trimmed, plus trimming projectors.test.ts and compose.test.ts) -- not scope creep, a strict necessary consequence of removing the two functions (otherwise vitest would newly fail on missing imports), called out explicitly since it wasn't itemized in the ticket text. (2) I found but did NOT remove: attachCacheStats/attachReuseStats/StepCacheStats/StepReuseStats in step-result.ts (the write-side counterpart of the reads I removed -- already had zero callers before my change, since their only producers, the extract/validate steps, were already deleted by C5; not named in my item list, and removing a producer-side symbol-channel API felt outside 'the dead reads and the RunSummary fields they feed'); and the dangling `memoryJunkWarning, DEFAULT_MEMORY_JUNK_FRACTION_WARN` import in index.ts (imported, never called -- pre-existing from C5, not something my edits caused, and not part of the config-orphan check's literal scope even though it's circumstantial dossier for item 3). (3) The most significant deviation: projectRetrievalQuality in run-summary/projectors.ts is now provably dead-input code on both of its inputs (retrieve-graph-build.ts deleted; the surviving retrieve step no longer emits quality_verdict at all) -- see noteIdFootprint for the full reasoning. This is why the literal grep gate command still lists run-summary/projectors.ts even though projectNoteFunnel and projectEventImpact are both fully gone. I left it untouched since it was not named in my assigned scope and its removal would need its own required-vs-optional schema check on RunSummary.retrieval_quality, the same kind of decision item 2 walked through for note_funnel/event_impact -- recommend a follow-up ticket. (4) No changes to git state (no add/commit/push) per instructions; all edits are uncommitted in the worktree."
